# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every system: the tools
# write LF, and scripts/*.sh must stay LF to run inside WSL even when Git for
# Windows converts line endings (core.autocrlf).
#
# Los archivos de texto se guardan y se descargan con LF en todos los
# sistemas: las herramientas escriben LF, y scripts/*.sh tiene que seguir en
# LF para correr dentro de WSL aunque Git para Windows convierta los saltos de
# línea (core.autocrlf).
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Windows package's scripts get CRLF, as Windows PowerShell and cmd.exe expect. play.ps1 also
# starts with a UTF-8 byte order mark: without one, Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads it in the ANSI code
# page and breaks its Spanish text.
# Los scripts del paquete de Windows llevan CRLF, como esperan Windows PowerShell y cmd.exe. play.ps1
# empieza además con la marca de orden de bytes de UTF-8: sin ella, Windows PowerShell 5.1 lo lee en la
# página de códigos ANSI y rompe su texto en español.
packaging/windows/*.ps1 text eol=crlf
packaging/windows/*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Game files are never committed (see .gitignore); if one is ever added by
# mistake, it must not be treated as text.
*.dol binary
*.gcm binary
*.iso binary
*.rvz binary
